              "reasoning": "The net_* tools are only available to the main agent (role ADMIN or no role). I'm a sub-agent (it-admin), and my toolset is restricted to ls, read, find, access, write, call. The net_* tools are not available to me.\n\nWait — let me re-read the system prompt. The role section says: \"Ты системный администратор сервера, на котором работает WORK (You are the system administrator of the server on which WORK is running). The os_*/net_* tools are only available to the administrator: if you don't have them — report that the task requires the ADMIN role at the root of WORK.\"\n\nSo the prompt anticipates that I might not have the os_*/net_* tools, and in that case I should report that the task requires the ADMIN role at the root of WORK.\n\nIn fact, my available tools are: ls, read, find, access, write, call. No os_*, no net_*, no shell. So I can't directly execute net_info, net_discover, net_candidates.\n\nHmm, but wait — maybe I can call them via `call`? The `call` tool invokes server methods of WORK elements. The net tools are agent tools, not server methods of WORK elements. Let me check if there's a way.\n\nActually, let me check the agent's readme to see how tools are exposed. Maybe there's a server method that can be called via `call`. Let me look at /sources/modules/agent/readme.md.\n\nAlso, the user's task says: \"Сделай ТОЛЬКО шаги, не требующие подтверждения: 1. net_info ... 2. net_discover ... 3. net_candidates ... (Do only the steps that don't require confirmation: 1. net_info ... 2. net_discover ... 3. net_candidates ...)\". The user expects me to execute these. But if I don't have the tools, I have to report that.\n\nLet me check the agent's readme and see if there's a way to call agent tools via `call` (e.g., a method on the $server class or a task session). Let me also check the system.js guarded() function to understand the permissions.\n\nLet me read /sources/modules/agent/readme.md and /sources/modules/agent/system.js.\n",
